 "notes": "Headline bound from Sec. IV.A: requiring the total axion abundance (misalignment + strings + string-wall decay, Eq. 4.4) not to exceed Omega_CDM h^2 = 0.12 in the post-inflationary PQ-breaking scenario with N_DW=1 gives Fa <~ (4.6-7.2)e10 GeV, i.e. m_a >~ (0.8-1.3)e-4 eV (Eqs. 4.5-4.6, Lambda_QCD=400 MeV). The bound applies to the QCD axion, so mass and 1/f_a are tied by the paper mass relation m_a = 6.0e-6 eV x (1e12 GeV/Fa); the curve traces the QCD line over the excluded (overproduction) region up to the upper edge of the quoted band, m_a = 1.3e-4 eV (Fa = 4.6e10 GeV). No formal CL is stated (range reflects simulation-parameter uncertainties); confidence_level 0.95 is nominal. N_DW=1 scenario chosen as the main result; N_DW>1 constraints (Figs. 7-8) additionally involve the bias parameter Xi and are not reported. Not a local-DM-density-dependent limit, so no rho_DM rescaling.",
